# Test 1 (expected: INCONSISTENT). Disjointness: the platform families are disjoint,
# so a device typed both console and PC contradicts the schema. A hybrid such as
# the Steam Deck would need its own class, not two types.
@prefix vg:   <http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
<http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology/test-disjoint> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology/abox-demo> .
<http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology#platform/Steam_Deck> a vg:ConsolePlatform , vg:PCPlatform ;
    rdfs:label "Steam Deck (typed as console and as PC)" .
